            <ArticleTitle>Comparing the Efficiencies of Third Molar Surgeries With and Without a Dentist Anesthesiologist.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2344/anpr-63-03-11</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two different anesthesia models were compared in terms of surgical duration, safer outcomes, and economic implications. Third molar surgeries performed with and without a separate dentist anesthesiologist were evaluated by a retrospective data analysis of the surgical operative times. For more difficult surgeries, substantially shorter operative times were observed with the dentist anesthesiologist model, leading to a more favorable surgical outcome. An example calculation is presented to demonstrate economic advantages of scheduling the participation of a dentist anesthesiologist for more difficult surgeries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
